# install/argsh.pin — which argsh runtime is bundled into docs/public/lo-up.
#
# The bundle is a build product of install/lo-up PLUS the argsh runtime
# sources, and it embeds the runtime's version and commit. Until this file
# existed the runtime revision was whatever the last person to run
# install/build happened to have checked out, which made "rebuild and diff"
# impossible to run anywhere else — the one gate that would catch a stale
# published installer.
#
# Read by install/build (which refuses to build from any other revision) and
# by the loup-bundle job in .github/workflows/ci.yml (which checks argsh out
# at `ref`, downloads the pinned minifier, rebuilds, and diffs). The rebuild
# is byte-exact: verified from a clean checkout with the released minifier.
#
# To bump the runtime:
#   git -C <argsh> checkout <new-ref>
#   ARGSH_PIN_UPDATE=1 ARGSH_SRC=<argsh> install/build
#   # then commit install/argsh.pin AND docs/public/lo-up together
#
# RISK, known and accepted for now: `ref` below is NOT on argsh's main branch.
# It sits on `feat/process-trace-phase2`, an unmerged feature branch, so the
# published installer bundles a runtime built from one. If that branch is
# force-pushed, rebased or deleted in arg-sh/argsh, the commit becomes
# unreachable and the loup-bundle CI job fails at the `actions/checkout` step
# with "Could not find the ref" — NOT at the diff, and nothing about the message
# will mention this file. That is the symptom; this is the cause.
#
# If you are reading this because CI just broke that way: the fix is to pick a
# reachable argsh revision (main, or a tag) and bump the pin with the procedure
# below, committing install/argsh.pin and docs/public/lo-up together. Moving the
# pin onto a merged revision is the real fix and is tracked separately.
#
# minifier_release / minifier_sha256 are for CI only — `argsh minify` shells
# out to the `minifier` binary, which is a Rust crate in the argsh repo and is
# published as a release asset. install/build uses whatever minifier is on
# PATH; CI pins the asset so the rebuild is reproducible there.

ref=a7b0295e62c708d7fe237252f8422576233cc8fa
describe=v0.10.0-30-ga7b0295
minifier_release=v0.10.0
minifier_sha256=6d8c915a03ff277e7e4722be73b273e7367eeaa086834cf45567d3327afd6156
